# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Optional environment variable reference (pi-vs-cc)
#
#  NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED for ordinary Pi use. Pi stores provider
#  authentication itself (including OAuth) — an already-authenticated
#  installation needs no project .env, no copied keys, and no new sign-in.
#
#  This file documents variable names only. Every line is commented out;
#  there are no placeholder keys to fill in. If you deliberately choose
#  environment-based configuration, export variables from your shell or
#  create a local .env (gitignored) and load it explicitly.
#
#  Note: Bun loads .env automatically unless --no-env-file is passed.
#  The justfile recipes pass --no-env-file so configuration stays
#  explicit; run `bun scripts/coms-net-server.ts` directly if you want
#  Bun's implicit .env behavior.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Model provider API keys (optional) ──────────────────────────────
# Only relevant if you prefer environment keys over Pi's saved
# credentials. See the Pi providers documentation for all supported
# providers and their variables.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── Firecrawl (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the pi-pi expert agents for web crawling. They fall back to
# curl when it is unset or the CLI is unavailable.
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# ── coms-net — HTTP/SSE Pi-to-Pi communication hub (optional) ───────
# Only needed when running the coms-net extension or server.

# Shared secret. Required to bind a LAN/remote server. For 127.0.0.1-only
# operation the server auto-generates a token and writes it to
# ~/.pi/coms-net/projects/<project>/server.secret.json. Set this to a long
# random string (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) before exposing the hub
# beyond localhost.
# PI_COMS_NET_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Pin the server port so the URL stays stable across restarts.
# Leave unset (or 0) to let the OS claim a free port.
# PI_COMS_NET_PORT=

# Hub URL for clients. Leave unset to auto-discover via server.json.
# Set to e.g. https://coms.example.com when connecting to a remote hub.
# PI_COMS_NET_SERVER_URL=
